<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13152" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-pālo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to mark off</i> or <i>bound
				with palings</i> (late Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jugera agri..ita uti depalatum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3688</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to found,
			establish</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quodammodo mundum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Herm. 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civitatem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Apol. 10</span></i>
			; cf. depalator.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
